# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to converting LF to CRLF on checkout, which is where those
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings come from. Left alone it causes diffs that
# show every line as changed when a Windows and a Linux machine touch the same file.
#
# This pins LF everywhere - in the repository AND in the working copy. Python, YAML,
# and shell scripts all prefer it, and CI runs on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
